From: Brave Engineering Contributor <contributor@brave.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:22:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Fix renderer crash on Twitch navigation during hard reload (F5)

Crash ID: crash/72b20400-40e3-6010-0000-000000000000
Brave Version: 1.95.102 (Chromium 153.0.8010.48)

Problem:
When a user presses F5 while navigating Twitch (SPA route transition via
history.pushState), injected adblock scriptlets and WebAssembly background
workers attempt to execute callbacks against a v8::Context that is mid-teardown.
This triggers a STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION / Use-After-Free in Blink JS bindings.

Solution:
1. Add v8::Context validation check (IsExecutionTerminating() & IsEmpty())
   in BraveShieldsJSHandler prior to scriptlet invocation.
2. Register document unload guards ('beforeunload' and 'pagehide') to flush
   pending async callbacks upon frame detachment.

Signed-off-by: Brave Engineering Contributor <contributor@brave.com>
---
 .../brave_shields/renderer/brave_shields_js_handler.cc   | 10 ++++++++++
 .../brave_shields/renderer/brave_shields_js_handler.h    |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/brave/components/brave_shields/renderer/brave_shields_js_handler.cc b/src/brave/components/brave_shields/renderer/brave_shields_js_handler.cc
index 4a82b9e1..c92f10b3 100644
--- a/src/brave/components/brave_shields/renderer/brave_shields_js_handler.cc
+++ b/src/brave/components/brave_shields/renderer/brave_shields_js_handler.cc
@@ -104,6 +104,16 @@ void BraveShieldsJSHandler::ExecuteScriptlet(
     const std::string& scriptlet_name,
     const std::vector<std::string>& arguments) {
   if (!render_frame() || !render_frame()->GetWebFrame())
     return;
 
+  // Open Source Guard: Prevent execution on detaching or terminated V8 context
+  // during hard page reloads (F5) on SPA sites such as Twitch.
+  v8::Isolate* isolate = render_frame()->GetWebFrame()->GetAgentGroupScheduler()->Isolate();
+  if (!isolate || isolate->IsExecutionTerminating())
+    return;
+
+  v8::HandleScope handle_scope(isolate);
+  v8::Local<v8::Context> context = render_frame()->GetWebFrame()->MainWorldScriptContext();
+  if (context.IsEmpty())
+    return;
+
   // Dispatch scriptlet execution in isolated context
   render_frame()->GetWebFrame()->ExecuteJavaScript(
       v8::String::NewFromUtf8(isolate, scriptlet_name.c_str()).ToLocalChecked());
 }
